#%PAM-1.0
#
# Let polkit accept a fingerprint, falling back to the password.
#
# This file shadows the one polkit ships at /usr/lib/pam.d/polkit-1, which is
# the same four `include system-auth` lines without the first one here.
# Overriding in /etc means a polkit update cannot silently drop the change, and
# reverting is deleting one file.
#
# Scoped to polkit on purpose. The password prompts worth removing are the ones
# pkexec and the KDE agent raise; login and sudo are left alone, so a sensor
# that stops working - a kernel update, a driver rebuild, an unplugged reader -
# can never lock anyone out of the machine.
#
# max-tries=20, timeout=90: the module's own defaults are 3 tries and 30
# seconds, which is tuned for a reliable reader, not this one. Measured over
# seven verify attempts on this sensor, five matched (scores 77-2920 against a
# threshold of 72) and two did not (0, 7) - about a 70% chance per touch, most
# of the miss being a placement that does not overlap any enrolled sample
# rather than a bad reading. Independent tries compound fast: at 70% per try,
# the chance every one of twenty fails is 0.3^20, on the order of 1 in
# 30,000,000. Raising the try count is what actually fixes the practical
# success rate here - the per-touch odds do not change, but the number of
# chances to clear them does. 90 seconds covers 20 tries comfortably even with
# a few retry-scan prompts mixed in; a lower number would cut tries short
# before they were used.
# `sufficient` is what makes that safe here too: if pam_fprintd fails for any
# reason, PAM carries on to system-auth and asks for the password exactly as
# before. It never turns a working prompt into a broken one.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -Dm644 polkit-1 /etc/pam.d/polkit-1
#
# Remove:
#   sudo rm /etc/pam.d/polkit-1
#
# No daemon restart is needed; PAM reads the stack per authentication.

auth       sufficient   pam_fprintd.so max-tries=20 timeout=90
auth       include      system-auth
account    include      system-auth
password   include      system-auth
session    include      system-auth
